# react-ui-feed — consolidation spec

Status: draft for the post-spike refactor. The spike answered "can one anchor-placed window scroll
smoothly with a CodeMirror editor per row" (yes — see `DESIGN.md` for the principles and
`TESTING.md` for the manual evidence). This document specifies what to keep, what to extract, and
the seams to cut so the parts are reusable across the project.

Naming below: **virtualizer** = the extracted placement engine (`placement.ts` + `useWindow`);
**list** = the message feed built on it (`MessageList`); **outliner** = the index-space rail
(`Outline`, currently in `react-ui-components`); **minimap** = the content-space rail.

---

## 1. Virtualizer

The reusable core. No DOM types in the model layer, no React in the placement layer, no knowledge
of messages anywhere. Target: extractable as `@dxos/react-ui-virtualizer` (or a `react-ui-list`
aspect) and usable by `react-ui-mosaic`'s `VirtualStack`, tables, and any long feed.

- **Placement model (`Placement`)** — pure arithmetic, fully unit-testable
  - One authoritative **anchor** (`id`, `index`, `start`); every other position derived by summing
    extents away from it
    - prepend shifts the anchor's index, never its position → nothing on screen moves
    - re-anchoring preserves every derived position exactly
  - **Extents, not heights** — scalars along one axis; the axis is the binding's business
    - host supplies `Extents { of(index), exact? }`; `exact` = never revised by measurement
      (deterministic layouts: fixed-height rows, declared-width cards) but still *checked* in dev
      (`onMismatch`)
    - measurements keyed by **row id**, not index — reordering or prepending cannot corrupt them
  - **Scroll & range**
    - `scrollTo(offset)` moves only the mounted range; corrections never touch the scroll
    - visible range vs mounted range reported separately (readouts describe the reader, not the
      overscan)
    - `overscan` option: rows to mount before/beyond the visible window, per side (default 8)
  - **Edges are ground truth**
    - `drift()` reports estimate error at start/end; reported, never silently applied
    - `endOffset()` / `offsetOf(index, align)` — derived from the anchor so asking where the end is
      does not move it
  - **Reserve** — empty extent after the last row (`scrollPastEnd` in host terms)
    - a *number the host computes*, added to the sizer; nothing else in the engine knows about it
    - this is what the tanstack design could not express (spacer lived outside the virtualizer's
      coordinate space — the two-coordinate-systems defect class)
- **DOM binding (`useWindow`)** — React hook against an element the *host* owns
  - three-element shape: scroller (host's), sizer (extent only, no rows), window (one absolutely
    positioned parent, moved by `transform`; rows unpositioned, in flow)
    - rows in flow → a row that changes extent reflows its followers in the browser, same frame
    - `overflow-anchor: none` on the scroller — exactly one party anchors
  - measures rows after every commit (`data-index` / `data-object-id` contract on row elements)
  - **sticky/follow** is an *intent*, withdrawn only by a backwards scroll — never re-derived from
    proximity (corrections grow the document under a stationary reader)
  - `WindowController.scrollToIndex(index, align, behavior)` — smooth only across mounted rows;
    far targets jump (a glide over unmounted content is a journey over a blank screen)
  - publishes `WindowState { index, visible, mounted, count, geometry }` — geometry in pixels for
    maps/rails, indices for readouts
  - axis-neutral: `block | inline`; only the binding maps extent→height/width
- **`Window`** — the trivial binding (own scroller div) for stories, tests, and simple hosts
- **Open items**
  - variable-size *reserve at the start* (pinned headers / date separators) — not yet needed
  - `estimateSize` naming: converge on `extents` everywhere (list still says `estimateSize`)
  - imperative `measure(id, extent)` for hosts that know a row changed (widget expanded) before
    layout runs

## 2. List

`MessageList` — the chat feed. Owns model-mapping and interaction; delegates all geometry to the
virtualizer. Composite: `Root` (headless) / `Viewport` (DOM) / `Item`.

- **Rendering**
  - `renderer(message) → ItemContent` resolves each message to a kind; **pluggable block
    renderers** keyed by kind: `markdown` (CodeMirror, read-only, shared cached extension sets),
    `html`, `custom` (host component), room for `json`, transcript, tool-call blocks
  - **Chrome is a host render-prop** (`Chrome` component: avatar, timestamp, fork/resolve
    controls); engine renders content only — chrome must not affect the measurement contract
    beyond being inside the measured row
  - **Widgets** (XML tags → React via registry): portaled into editor decorations; state owned by
    `Root`-level store so it survives row unmount/remount; expansion is *not* a special case —
    it is the same measurement arriving again (post-commit measure pass)
  - `Column` three-track layout (gutter | content | gutter) inside the row, not on the container
- **Row selection**
  - today: set-of-ids + additive click, one `SelectionGroup` for text selection across editors
  - spec: extract a **selection controller/model** with interchangeable policies —
    `single`, `multi` (toggle), `range` (shift-click, anchor+focus over the *anchors* sequence);
    align with `react-ui-list` Listbox semantics (`aria-selected`, `dx-selected`) so styling and
    a11y come from one place
  - selection is model-space (ids), never DOM-space — must survive virtualization
- **Navigation**
  - **pluggable stops**: `isAnchor(message, index)` today; generalize to a `stops` provider —
    per message, per prompt (user turns only), per block, per search hit, per day divider
  - one mechanism for every driver: toolbar buttons, arrow keys, outliner, minimap all call the
    same `step(delta)` / `jumpTo(stop)`; **common event/controller** shared with the outliner
    (see §3) rather than parallel wiring
  - cursor = row containing the scroll offset (derived, never set alongside the scroll) — this is
    what makes every press travel
  - Cmd/Ctrl+Arrow = first/last; keymap bound to the viewport element (focusable, tabIndex=0)
- **Scrolling**
  - smooth for steps within the mounted window; instant for far jumps — *policy lives in the
    controller, not in each caller*
  - `smooth vs jump` is a per-call `behavior`, with a host default
- **Follow (streaming)**
  - sticky intent as in §1; opt-out = backwards scroll, opt-in = returning to the tail
  - `ScrollFollower` (velocity-based glide, rows/s, median row height) exists with tests but is
    **not wired** post-swap — decision pending manual verdict on whether instant correction reads
    as abrupt (TESTING.md §2.6); if wired, it drives the element and the placement follows via
    scroll events
- **Toolbar / statusbar**
  - engine renders neither; `useMessageList()` exposes state (`range`, `currentIndex`, counts,
    jumps/shifts diagnostics) and controls (`stepAnchor`, `scrollToIndex`, `scrollToBottom`)
  - stories' toolbar/statusbar are the reference consumers; product chrome lives in
    plugin-assistant
- **Options**
  - `debug` (row outlines + extents, jump detector), `scrollPastEnd` (reserve), `overscan`,
    `stickyBottom`, `estimateSize | (message, index) => extent`, `streamingId`, `hits`
  - all off-by-default; `debug` never defaults true

## 3. Outliner

Index-space rail: one tick per *stop* (not per row). Currently `Outline` in `react-ui-components`.

- **Model**
  - markers `{ id, title, description?, range }` in the host's own position space; thinning to
    fit fixed tick pitch (8px), each tick standing for the span to the next
  - active = marker intersecting `visibleRange`
- **Interaction**
  - hover: wave extension + one popover card tracking the tick's center (separate zero-height
    anchor; ticks never wrapped — element identity must be stable)
  - two "at a tick" states, kept apart and published (`data-pointer`, `data-navigated`,
    `data-shown`): pointer wins while pointing; keyboard wins while navigating; pointing again
    hands back
  - dismissal: tick-level leave + document-level `pointerover` backstop (popover focus guards eat
    the leave after a click)
- **Navigation unification (the spec change)**
  - `onNavigate(delta)` / `onSelect(marker)` today; replace both with the **same navigation
    controller the toolbar uses** — outliner emits intents (`step(±1)`, `jumpTo(stop)`), the list
    executes, the outliner re-derives its shown tick from `visibleRange`
  - stops shown by the outliner = the list's pluggable stops (§2), so a "per prompt" feed shows
    per-prompt ticks with no extra wiring
- **Options**: `tickSize` (8), `width` (2rem), classNames; centred ticks; bounded-vs-natural height

## 4. Minimap

Content-space rail: the document in miniature. Currently `testing/debug/Minimap` — promote to a
real component next to `Outline`.

- **Model** — drawn from `WindowState.geometry` only
  - track = total extent (reserve included); faint band = mounted window; solid band = viewport
  - invariant to watch: viewport band ⊆ mounted band (viewport outside mounted = reader looking
    at nothing)
- **Interaction**
  - click/drag → jump to that *fraction* of content space (emits fraction; host maps to offset via
    the controller — same navigation seam as §3)
  - optional hover readout (index at fraction) once navigation is unified
- **Options**: `width` (2rem, matching Outline — asserted), no rounded corners, orientation follows
  the list's axis
- Debug-only overlays (per-row extents, drift markers) stay in `testing/debug`

---

## 5. Precedents and retrofit

- **react-ui-list**
  - `useListNavigation` (tabster) is *focus* navigation for fully-mounted lists; the feed's
    navigation is *scroll* navigation over mostly-unmounted rows — different problem, keep both,
    but adopt its role/ARIA conventions (`listbox`/`option`, `dx-selected`) for the selection
    model in §2
  - Listbox's opt-in selection semantics are the pattern the selection controller should present
- **react-ui-mosaic**
  - `VirtualStack` still runs tanstack react-virtual — the same engine the feed just removed, with
    the same defect class available to it; **retrofit candidate**: bind `useWindow` under
    `VirtualStack` (it already owns its scroller), keeping its pagination hook
    (`useVirtualizerPagination` becomes an `onEdge('start'|'end')` consumer — edge callbacks are
    already in the placement API)
  - do this *after* the feed has soaked; mosaic adds drag-and-drop, which the spike never exercised
- **Suggested order**
  1. extract virtualizer (placement + useWindow + Window) to its own entry point with the tests
  2. navigation controller (list ⇄ outliner ⇄ minimap on one seam)
  3. selection controller (single/multi/range policies)
  4. promote Minimap; move Outline next to it
  5. mosaic retrofit behind a flag
